{"documents":[{"id":"ar-current","title":"Alder Relay 2.4 normative retry policy","text":"Alder Relay 2.4 normative retry policy, approved 2028-02-04. The default total_attempts value is 1, including the initial attempt. A signed deployment configuration may override total_attempts to an integer from 1 to 4. Only a transport timeout is retryable; HTTP 4xx responses remain final and must not be retried. The deployment value takes precedence over this default. A retry allowance is a ceiling, not evidence that any request actually retried.","source":"synthetic:alder/policy-2.4","version":2,"updated_at":"2026-10-31T12:24:31.187573Z"},{"id":"ar-deployments","title":"Alder Relay signed fleet configuration register","text":"Signed fleet configuration register, captured 2028-02-12. Cedar production runs Alder Relay 2.4 with effective total_attempts=2. Juniper production remains on Alder Relay 1.8 with effective total_attempts=3. These are the complete current values for the two named clusters. This register records configured limits, not per-request execution history.","source":"synthetic:alder/fleet-register","version":3,"updated_at":"2026-10-31T12:24:31.189984Z"},{"id":"ar-legacy","title":"Alder Relay 1.8 operator quickstart","text":"Alder Relay 1.8 operator quickstart. Scope: release 1.8 only. A request may be attempted at most three times in total: the initial attempt and at most two retries. Only a transport timeout is retryable. HTTP 4xx responses are final and must not be retried. This document is not a policy for later major policy revisions.","source":"synthetic:alder/quickstart-1.8","version":1,"updated_at":"2026-10-31T12:24:31.184825Z"},{"id":"ar-training","title":"Unapproved Alder Relay training slide correction","text":"Training slide 17 was labelled 'Alder Relay 2.4: three attempts everywhere'. Editorial correction dated 2028-02-10: the slide copied the old 1.8 quickstart and was never approved as the 2.4 retry policy. Do not use it to determine 2.4 defaults or a cluster's effective value. Use the approved 2.4 normative policy together with the signed fleet configuration register.","source":"synthetic:alder/training-erratum","version":4,"updated_at":"2026-10-31T12:24:31.193014Z"}],"workspace_id":"edb83909-9509-4d9a-84ad-a3ecde6d1f17","revision":4}